WEBVTT

00:00:06.550 --> 00:00:08.990
Please teach me how to battle.

00:00:08.990 --> 00:00:10.200
Shock.

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:11.550
Where is this coming from?

00:00:11.550 --> 00:00:13.920
I've thought about a lot of stuff in my own way,

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:15.960
and I decided that I have to be stronger.

00:00:16.470 --> 00:00:18.600
Please, master!

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:19.710
Confusion.

00:00:19.710 --> 00:00:20.660
Please...

00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:21.520
Refusal.

00:00:22.420 --> 00:00:23.390
Busy.

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:26.380
I have no time to help others.

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:29.440
Just in your free time...

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:30.660
No.

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:32.980
Then I'll pay you for lessons.

00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:37.940
Um, for example, have you 
heard of Monjiya's daifuku?

00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:39.200
Favorite.

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:41.310
There's always a line, isn't there?

00:00:41.310 --> 00:00:43.920
I'll stand in line and get some for you!

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:45.270
How about that?

00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:46.410
Consideration.

00:00:46.910 --> 00:00:50.110
If you could do it...

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:52.420
Thank you!

00:00:52.420 --> 00:00:53.680
Early.

00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:56.160
Shouldn't you be happy when 
you've acquired them?

00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:57.280
You're right.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:34.000
Evolution / Pure White and Pitch Black

00:02:41.630 --> 00:02:45.760
The next two targets are inexperienced.

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:48.020
Which will you hit first?

00:02:48.020 --> 00:02:50.350
Chinatsu-chan, you can pick.

00:02:58.630 --> 00:03:00.150
Good luck.

00:03:03.990 --> 00:03:05.700
All right, thanks.

00:03:10.930 --> 00:03:17.170
So, try to understand which synergy 
cards work with your deck.

00:03:17.980 --> 00:03:19.050
Like...

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:23.680
If I do this, the effect is doubled?

00:03:24.550 --> 00:03:25.380
Yes.

00:03:26.020 --> 00:03:29.310
That's called a "combo." You're 
pretty smart to pick up on it.

00:03:30.050 --> 00:03:31.270
I got a compliment!

00:03:31.270 --> 00:03:33.380
Shall we call it a day?

00:03:33.380 --> 00:03:35.900
Yes, thank you.

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:36.770
All right, then.

00:03:37.600 --> 00:03:40.280
Master, here's your lesson fee.

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:41.430
Joy!

00:03:42.390 --> 00:03:44.300
Nice job getting me these.

00:03:44.300 --> 00:03:46.680
I stood in line forever.

00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:49.540
And they sold out right after I left.

00:03:49.540 --> 00:03:51.260
That was close.

00:03:51.260 --> 00:03:53.340
Sounds like a rough time.

00:03:53.340 --> 00:03:57.560
But this was your idea.

00:03:57.560 --> 00:03:58.750
That's right.

00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:01.050
It's so good!

00:04:04.060 --> 00:04:05.260
Doubt.

00:04:05.260 --> 00:04:07.140
I want to ask you something.

00:04:07.140 --> 00:04:08.400
Sure, what is it?

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:11.830
You were never interested in battles before.

00:04:11.830 --> 00:04:15.810
Does your sudden desire to be strong 
have to do with Chinatsu-san?

00:04:16.420 --> 00:04:17.680
Yeah.

00:04:17.680 --> 00:04:19.480
I understand now.

00:04:19.480 --> 00:04:24.390
Chi-chan really wants to be rid of me.

00:04:25.920 --> 00:04:27.070
Doubt.

00:04:27.070 --> 00:04:28.940
Even if you get stronger,

00:04:28.940 --> 00:04:31.200
if Chinatsu-chan wins enough battles,

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:33.620
she'll give up her memories.

00:04:35.170 --> 00:04:37.030
That's right.

00:04:37.030 --> 00:04:39.210
That's why I want to be strong.

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:42.660
To protect both of our memories.

00:04:45.140 --> 00:04:45.840
<i>I...</i>

00:04:48.050 --> 00:04:50.350
See you tomorrow, too!

00:04:54.540 --> 00:04:55.390
Roger.

00:04:59.170 --> 00:05:02.230
Protect both of their memories, huh?

00:05:02.840 --> 00:05:04.440
So noble, isn't it?

00:05:04.440 --> 00:05:07.110
The lost puzzle pieces...

00:05:07.950 --> 00:05:10.120
I'm sure you won't tell me, will you?

00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:17.020
A stupid question, wasn't it?

00:05:18.350 --> 00:05:19.130
Shirai?

00:05:21.100 --> 00:05:22.550
Shirai, it's been a while!

00:05:23.820 --> 00:05:25.480
Why are you reacting like that?

00:05:25.480 --> 00:05:27.380
That's kind of a shock.

00:05:27.380 --> 00:05:29.430
Did you forget me?

00:05:30.060 --> 00:05:31.960
Well, I'm taller now...

00:05:35.580 --> 00:05:37.900
Hey, let's go home.

00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:40.860
What's wrong, Shou-chan?

00:05:42.110 --> 00:05:43.530
So that's how this works?

00:05:45.270 --> 00:05:46.780
Isn't that the boy from before?

00:05:47.620 --> 00:05:50.600
I heard that our memories would disappear,

00:05:50.600 --> 00:05:52.790
but I didn't really understand what it meant.

00:05:53.300 --> 00:05:55.160
The time limit's about to expire again.

00:05:55.630 --> 00:05:56.850
When that happens, you'll—

00:05:56.850 --> 00:06:02.110
This is the local soccer team 
I was on during elementary school.

00:06:02.110 --> 00:06:04.120
We won the city tournament.

00:06:04.570 --> 00:06:07.560
I contributed a lot to the team.

00:06:08.660 --> 00:06:10.010
And the coach...

00:06:10.580 --> 00:06:11.860
Shou-chan?

00:06:12.400 --> 00:06:13.560
I think I...

00:06:13.560 --> 00:06:15.250
Come on, let's fight the battles.

00:06:15.250 --> 00:06:17.090
Let's do it, Shou-chan!

00:06:17.870 --> 00:06:18.600
Battle...

00:06:20.570 --> 00:06:21.860
That's right.

00:06:25.020 --> 00:06:28.450
Master, here's your Momotae cheese tart.

00:06:28.680 --> 00:06:30.020
Good work.

00:06:30.870 --> 00:06:32.260
Exuberant.

00:06:32.260 --> 00:06:34.370
I never expected to get one.

00:06:34.370 --> 00:06:36.370
I was able to make reservations this time,

00:06:36.370 --> 00:06:38.200
but I could only get one.

00:06:38.200 --> 00:06:39.440
Sufficient!

00:06:39.440 --> 00:06:40.580
Thank you.

00:06:42.770 --> 00:06:43.540
Well?

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:45.590
Yeah, they're close.

00:06:49.380 --> 00:06:51.020
Well? Is it good?

00:06:51.020 --> 00:06:52.850
Want a bite?

00:06:52.850 --> 00:06:54.500
Really? No, I—

00:06:54.500 --> 00:06:55.390
No need to hold back.

00:06:55.730 --> 00:06:58.840
Besides, it's hard to eat with
you looking like that.

00:07:00.400 --> 00:07:02.810
Oh, I brought tea.

00:07:02.810 --> 00:07:04.760
Gratitude. How kind of you.

00:07:05.080 --> 00:07:05.660
Suzuko.

00:07:06.790 --> 00:07:08.020
They're close.

00:07:08.870 --> 00:07:11.030
Yes, I feel it, too.

00:07:19.410 --> 00:07:20.750
You're Selectors, right?

00:07:21.800 --> 00:07:24.450
You desire a battle with us?

00:07:24.450 --> 00:07:27.170
Ah, no, that's not it.

00:07:28.390 --> 00:07:29.880
Then what?

00:07:30.780 --> 00:07:31.680
Huh?

00:07:34.480 --> 00:07:36.240
You know him?

00:07:36.240 --> 00:07:38.620
We met once.

00:07:38.620 --> 00:07:39.640
It's been a while.

00:07:39.640 --> 00:07:40.720
Yeah.

00:07:41.360 --> 00:07:43.190
Is that yours?

00:07:44.600 --> 00:07:46.640
This belongs to a friend.

00:07:48.590 --> 00:07:51.430
Is your friend Morikawa Chinatsu?

00:07:52.320 --> 00:07:54.260
You know Chi-chan?

00:07:54.260 --> 00:07:56.500
Yeah, we went to the same middle school.

00:07:56.500 --> 00:07:57.580
I see!

00:07:58.180 --> 00:08:01.520
But why do you have that?

00:08:01.520 --> 00:08:04.040
Morikawa always had that on her.

00:08:04.040 --> 00:08:06.460
It seemed to be really important to her.

00:08:08.300 --> 00:08:09.800
I see!

00:08:12.380 --> 00:08:15.950
Your father said he'd be done 
with work by evening.

00:08:15.950 --> 00:08:18.240
So eat your dinner together, okay?

00:08:19.080 --> 00:08:20.940
I have work, too.

00:08:21.700 --> 00:08:22.890
I don't need dinner.

00:08:24.020 --> 00:08:25.410
You have work now?

00:08:25.410 --> 00:08:26.260
Yeah.

00:08:26.260 --> 00:08:27.910
A new job.

00:08:28.570 --> 00:08:30.070
What happened to the old one?

00:08:30.070 --> 00:08:31.120
I quit.

00:08:31.680 --> 00:08:32.490
Oh...

00:08:32.980 --> 00:08:35.240
So what job are you doing now?

00:08:36.020 --> 00:08:37.770
Sorry. I'm in a hurry.

00:08:38.360 --> 00:08:40.020
We'll talk when I get home.

00:08:40.530 --> 00:08:41.760
Chinatsu, wait—

00:08:41.760 --> 00:08:44.470
I'm not doing anything you have to worry about.

00:08:50.120 --> 00:08:52.050
So that's what happened?

00:08:52.280 --> 00:08:54.890
When she thought someone 
was in the wrong,

00:08:54.890 --> 00:08:59.680
whether it was an older student or 
a teacher, she'd stand up to them.

00:08:59.680 --> 00:09:01.520
Oh, yeah, I know.

00:09:01.520 --> 00:09:03.230
She's always been that way.

00:09:03.230 --> 00:09:06.890
That's why people started to 
think she was strong-willed.

00:09:07.690 --> 00:09:10.280
But really, she was a very nice girl.

00:09:10.280 --> 00:09:11.590
Suspicion.

00:09:11.590 --> 00:09:13.390
Did you have a crush on her?

00:09:14.060 --> 00:09:15.610
Of course not!

00:09:16.610 --> 00:09:21.600
Question. If you don't want to challenge 
me to a battle, what do you want?

00:09:22.050 --> 00:09:24.580
You didn't come to talk about 
old times, did you?

00:09:25.090 --> 00:09:27.620
No, I actually had a request.

00:09:28.020 --> 00:09:28.830
A request?

00:09:29.520 --> 00:09:30.910
Want to join me?

00:09:32.060 --> 00:09:33.590
What do you mean?

00:09:38.880 --> 00:09:41.640
I don't intend to battle.

00:09:42.880 --> 00:09:44.100
What do you mean?

00:09:45.400 --> 00:09:47.310
You and I can be partners

00:09:48.010 --> 00:09:50.040
and battle once in a while.

00:09:50.040 --> 00:09:53.720
We trade wins so we don't run out of coins.

00:09:54.210 --> 00:09:57.490
That way, when the ninety-day time limit ends,

00:09:57.490 --> 00:10:00.490
we can done with the battles 
and still have our coins.

00:10:00.490 --> 00:10:02.840
So that's your plan.

00:10:02.840 --> 00:10:03.940
Yeah.

00:10:04.920 --> 00:10:06.960
Well? Good idea, right?

00:10:08.340 --> 00:10:09.240
Rejection.

00:10:09.240 --> 00:10:11.220
I refuse your offer.

00:10:12.570 --> 00:10:13.130
Why?

00:10:13.650 --> 00:10:16.870
Just as you have a reason not to battle,

00:10:16.870 --> 00:10:21.040
I have a reason I must battle.

00:10:21.040 --> 00:10:21.680
What is it?

00:10:21.680 --> 00:10:23.780
I don't have to tell you that.

00:10:24.600 --> 00:10:27.460
And there's a gap in your logic.

00:10:27.890 --> 00:10:28.990
Explanation.

00:10:28.990 --> 00:10:31.420
Even if you control your wins 
and losses in the battles,

00:10:31.420 --> 00:10:33.700
each time you lose, a coin will blacken,

00:10:33.700 --> 00:10:35.960
and you'll lose memories.

00:10:36.360 --> 00:10:37.430
Suggestion.

00:10:37.430 --> 00:10:41.320
Also, we can't choose which memories we lose.

00:10:44.800 --> 00:10:45.870
Shou-chan...

00:10:46.940 --> 00:10:49.030
What? He'll help with the battles?

00:10:49.030 --> 00:10:49.820
Yes.

00:10:49.820 --> 00:10:51.940
Make a contract with the bookmaker,

00:10:51.940 --> 00:10:55.630
and he'll find you someone to 
fight whenever you need it.

00:10:56.020 --> 00:10:59.740
Isn't it hard to find someone to fight?

00:11:00.780 --> 00:11:02.900
It is, but...

00:11:03.430 --> 00:11:07.170
Why not have a battle right now?

00:11:08.040 --> 00:11:09.640
If you'll sign the contract,

00:11:09.640 --> 00:11:11.980
I'm willing to lose deliberately.

00:11:12.420 --> 00:11:13.230
Really?

00:11:14.110 --> 00:11:15.190
Yes.

00:11:16.100 --> 00:11:16.880
Open.

00:11:19.730 --> 00:11:20.740
I can win...

00:11:20.740 --> 00:11:21.740
Berserk.

00:11:22.390 --> 00:11:23.620
Turn end.

00:11:23.620 --> 00:11:25.380
There it is!

00:11:25.380 --> 00:11:26.260
I win!

00:11:26.260 --> 00:11:27.200
Full attack!

00:11:34.740 --> 00:11:38.960
I feel kind of bad for having 
you let me win like that.

00:11:40.200 --> 00:11:43.300
Please sign the contract, then.

00:11:43.800 --> 00:11:45.850
I don't know...

00:11:45.850 --> 00:11:49.580
You won't start asking me 
for money later, right?

00:11:49.580 --> 00:11:50.980
Of course not.

00:11:50.980 --> 00:11:53.340
I don't know... It seems shady.

00:11:53.960 --> 00:11:55.350
It's kind of scary.

00:11:55.350 --> 00:11:57.060
I'll pass.

00:12:00.840 --> 00:12:02.930
Wh-What are you doing?!

00:12:02.930 --> 00:12:04.280
Don't be a bitch.

00:12:04.830 --> 00:12:07.270
I sacrificed something for you.

00:12:10.250 --> 00:12:12.370
Don't think you can get away.

00:12:12.680 --> 00:12:14.120
Things aren't that easy.

00:12:14.120 --> 00:12:15.630
<b>Contract</b>

00:12:23.300 --> 00:12:24.420
Well?

00:12:24.420 --> 00:12:26.170
Did you get the contract?

00:12:26.170 --> 00:12:27.010
Yes.

00:12:27.010 --> 00:12:28.760
Way to go, Chinatsu-chan!

00:12:29.080 --> 00:12:29.980
Oh, right.

00:12:29.980 --> 00:12:32.650
Rio-chan's doing her best, too.

00:12:32.650 --> 00:12:34.800
Nice to meet you!

00:12:34.800 --> 00:12:35.880
Y-Yeah.

00:12:35.880 --> 00:12:37.750
You, too, Rio-chan.

00:12:38.240 --> 00:12:41.160
You're fighting a little girl like this?

00:12:42.120 --> 00:12:44.400
Onii-chan, no weird ideas 
about taking pity on her!

00:12:44.730 --> 00:12:45.740
I know.

00:12:45.740 --> 00:12:48.010
Aw, you say that...

00:12:48.490 --> 00:12:51.090
But you'd better not remember 
your sister and wimp out again!

00:12:51.090 --> 00:12:53.430
I'm the one who gets hurt!

00:12:53.430 --> 00:12:54.750
Y-Yeah.

00:12:55.300 --> 00:12:56.670
Okay, let's get started!

00:12:56.970 --> 00:12:58.040
Open!

00:12:58.040 --> 00:12:59.600
O-Open.

00:13:06.650 --> 00:13:08.550
I have two coins left.

00:13:08.890 --> 00:13:10.810
If I use one and lose one, it's game over—

00:13:10.810 --> 00:13:13.510
Stop whining to yourself, and grow me!

00:13:13.510 --> 00:13:15.250
Right. Grow.

00:13:15.250 --> 00:13:17.680
Summon two SIGNI Browcras.

00:13:17.680 --> 00:13:18.580
Turn end.

00:13:19.210 --> 00:13:20.590
Mommy, grow.

00:13:21.120 --> 00:13:23.640
Do the usual!

00:13:23.640 --> 00:13:25.240
Summon two Fermats and...

00:13:25.790 --> 00:13:27.530
Turn end!

00:13:28.430 --> 00:13:30.120
The usual?

00:13:30.120 --> 00:13:31.040
What's that?

00:13:31.040 --> 00:13:32.820
Just attack!

00:13:32.820 --> 00:13:34.730
Nothing happens on the first turn!

00:13:34.730 --> 00:13:35.580
Right.

00:13:35.580 --> 00:13:37.330
Aya, grow.

00:13:37.330 --> 00:13:38.710
Full attack!

00:13:46.240 --> 00:13:48.700
Oh, dear... That hurt.

00:13:48.700 --> 00:13:50.220
Mommy, are you okay?

00:13:50.220 --> 00:13:52.680
That was mean! You're so violent, Onii-chan!

00:13:53.400 --> 00:13:54.960
That's the one word he can't stand.

00:13:54.960 --> 00:13:56.080
It's my turn!

00:13:56.080 --> 00:13:57.230
Mommy, grow!

00:13:57.770 --> 00:13:59.520
All right, Rio-chan.

00:13:59.960 --> 00:14:01.890
Summon Minu and Plus!

00:14:02.470 --> 00:14:04.550
And coin bet, Mommy.

00:14:09.520 --> 00:14:10.320
Cheating.

00:14:10.320 --> 00:14:12.180
Here we go, Onii-chan!

00:14:12.180 --> 00:14:13.410
Attack!

00:14:24.830 --> 00:14:25.340
Huh?

00:14:25.580 --> 00:14:26.970
Is that her ability?

00:14:29.830 --> 00:14:32.670
Now, it's our turn, Onii-chan!

00:14:32.670 --> 00:14:33.600
Yeah.

00:14:33.600 --> 00:14:36.900
Grow, and... attack...

00:14:38.530 --> 00:14:41.360
Hurry up and attack, you scumbag sister-lover!

00:14:41.360 --> 00:14:43.980
Mommy, what's a "scumbag sister-lover"?

00:14:43.980 --> 00:14:47.250
Rio-chan, you don't need 
to learn words like that.

00:14:47.250 --> 00:14:49.650
Also, it means people like him.

00:14:50.420 --> 00:14:55.450
Att-att-att... Att-attack...

00:15:05.830 --> 00:15:06.800
We did it!

00:15:06.800 --> 00:15:08.170
You fell for it, Onii-chan!

00:15:08.480 --> 00:15:09.930
Onii-chan...

00:15:09.930 --> 00:15:12.390
With that innocent smile...

00:15:16.650 --> 00:15:18.180
Thank you very much!

00:15:19.570 --> 00:15:21.440
Good work, Rio-chan.

00:15:21.440 --> 00:15:22.890
I'm glad you won!

00:15:22.890 --> 00:15:24.350
Are you okay with this?

00:15:22.890 --> 00:15:25.610
Yeah! Mommy, let's do our 
best next time, too!

00:15:24.350 --> 00:15:26.510
You'll disappear, like your little sister!

00:15:26.510 --> 00:15:28.680
Do you understand that?!

00:15:29.630 --> 00:15:31.150
Don't say that.

00:15:35.960 --> 00:15:38.210
This isn't the right brand.

00:15:38.210 --> 00:15:39.080
I told you last time.

00:15:40.250 --> 00:15:42.420
You can't even run errands,

00:15:42.420 --> 00:15:43.900
Sumida #2?

00:15:45.230 --> 00:15:46.630
Sorry.

00:15:48.300 --> 00:15:49.880
Go get the right ones.

00:15:49.880 --> 00:15:52.160
Right... Will do!

00:15:53.090 --> 00:15:54.640
<b>Contract</b>

00:15:53.340 --> 00:15:54.240
Here.

00:15:56.090 --> 00:15:58.420
You really are talented.

00:15:58.420 --> 00:15:59.890
Just as I expected.

00:16:01.250 --> 00:16:03.240
I'm sorry about last time...

00:16:03.750 --> 00:16:05.440
Your battle with Suzuko-chan.

00:16:06.140 --> 00:16:07.240
It doesn't matter.

00:16:07.760 --> 00:16:11.400
She may seem unable to do anything alone,

00:16:11.400 --> 00:16:14.280
but that girl has something about her.

00:16:14.280 --> 00:16:15.530
What do you mean by "something"?

00:16:15.760 --> 00:16:17.550
I couldn't say.

00:16:18.020 --> 00:16:21.360
Well, I guess it means she's not like you.

00:16:21.360 --> 00:16:23.620
She's stronger than I am?

00:16:23.620 --> 00:16:24.870
I didn't say that!

00:16:25.600 --> 00:16:26.760
But...

00:16:27.980 --> 00:16:31.220
You spoke of chains that tied you down,

00:16:31.220 --> 00:16:33.970
but aren't you the one tying yourself down?

00:16:33.970 --> 00:16:38.050
If you let your guard down, 
you might get swallowed up...

00:16:41.160 --> 00:16:42.550
Here, then.

00:16:42.550 --> 00:16:44.410
Your next target.

00:16:55.990 --> 00:16:58.900
And there's a gap in your logic.

00:16:58.900 --> 00:17:01.020
Each time you lose, a coin will blacken,

00:17:01.020 --> 00:17:03.300
and you'll lose memories.

00:17:03.300 --> 00:17:05.790
We can't choose which memories we lose.

00:17:15.760 --> 00:17:16.800
Morikawa?

00:17:17.300 --> 00:17:19.520
What are you doing here?

00:17:19.520 --> 00:17:21.930
I was looking for you, Shirai-kun.

00:17:23.350 --> 00:17:24.810
I'm glad I found you.

00:17:26.060 --> 00:17:28.270
I realized something...

00:17:28.570 --> 00:17:33.780
I thought that even if I lost some of 
my memories, I'd still be me.

00:17:34.340 --> 00:17:35.730
But that's wrong.

00:17:35.730 --> 00:17:36.920
I don't want to lose them.

00:17:38.590 --> 00:17:42.640
So I tried to think of a way around it,

00:17:43.210 --> 00:17:45.740
but I guess I can't get away.

00:17:46.220 --> 00:17:48.700
There's something you don't want to lose, then.

00:17:53.820 --> 00:17:56.400
In that case, want to do it with me?

00:17:58.530 --> 00:18:00.620
Am I not good enough?

00:18:12.930 --> 00:18:13.700
Here.

00:18:29.680 --> 00:18:30.660
Open.

00:18:41.980 --> 00:18:43.260
Donor, grow.

00:18:43.910 --> 00:18:45.450
Shou-chan, can you fight?

00:18:45.450 --> 00:18:46.360
Yeah.

00:18:46.930 --> 00:18:48.320
Summon Karakasa.

00:18:48.320 --> 00:18:49.630
Turn end.

00:18:49.630 --> 00:18:51.340
Meru, Ener Charge.

00:18:51.340 --> 00:18:52.390
Grow.

00:18:53.600 --> 00:18:55.050
Here I go!

00:18:55.050 --> 00:18:56.640
Turn end.

00:18:56.640 --> 00:18:58.040
Huh? Why?

00:18:58.040 --> 00:18:59.280
You'll be attacked!

00:18:59.910 --> 00:19:01.450
What are you thinking?

00:19:01.900 --> 00:19:03.950
You have a memory you 
don't want to lose, right?

00:19:05.000 --> 00:19:06.740
I'll let you win.

00:19:06.740 --> 00:19:07.860
A trap?

00:19:08.320 --> 00:19:10.250
But it doesn't look that way.

00:19:10.250 --> 00:19:11.880
Donor, grow.

00:19:12.480 --> 00:19:13.500
Why not attack?

00:19:14.740 --> 00:19:16.500
Donor, attack.

00:19:22.060 --> 00:19:23.140
Ow!

00:19:24.460 --> 00:19:26.280
You really aren't going to attack?

00:19:26.280 --> 00:19:27.250
That's right.

00:19:27.250 --> 00:19:29.760
You don't have many coins yourself!

00:19:29.760 --> 00:19:33.110
Shirai-kun's memories are more 
important than mine.

00:19:33.920 --> 00:19:34.770
Turn end.

00:19:35.280 --> 00:19:36.280
You're sure?

00:19:36.770 --> 00:19:38.350
Meru, Ener charge.

00:19:38.350 --> 00:19:38.780
Grow.

00:19:40.980 --> 00:19:42.130
Turn end.

00:19:44.060 --> 00:19:46.120
You're okay with this?

00:19:46.760 --> 00:19:49.060
I said I'd let you win, didn't I?

00:19:51.160 --> 00:19:52.600
Donor, grow.

00:19:54.350 --> 00:19:56.030
Apparition Snow Queen!

00:19:56.870 --> 00:19:58.980
Line it up with Nurari, 
and activate Layer effect.

00:19:58.980 --> 00:19:59.910
Attack!

00:20:11.720 --> 00:20:13.320
Oh, too bad.

00:20:14.140 --> 00:20:15.020
That's a Burst.

00:20:21.840 --> 00:20:22.540
Donor...

00:20:22.540 --> 00:20:25.550
This doesn't make sense. 
She's not planning on losing!

00:20:25.550 --> 00:20:27.780
Shou-chan, something's coming next turn!

00:20:28.140 --> 00:20:29.540
You should use your coin!

00:20:30.650 --> 00:20:31.660
You're kidding...

00:20:32.220 --> 00:20:32.910
Morikawa.

00:20:34.140 --> 00:20:36.830
Whose words will you believe?

00:20:38.720 --> 00:20:40.230
Coin bet.

00:20:42.940 --> 00:20:44.100
Escape!

00:20:45.070 --> 00:20:45.930
Turn end.

00:20:46.280 --> 00:20:46.800
Grow.

00:20:48.130 --> 00:20:49.950
Accessorize Steak with Teaksauce.

00:20:49.950 --> 00:20:51.470
Coin bet.

00:20:52.470 --> 00:20:53.480
Berserk.

00:20:55.860 --> 00:20:58.310
Disable Escape...

00:21:00.230 --> 00:21:01.110
Attack.

00:21:07.950 --> 00:21:10.340
ARTS: Dust Chute.

00:21:15.700 --> 00:21:16.420
Donor!

00:21:20.530 --> 00:21:22.380
Now the board is clear.

00:21:22.980 --> 00:21:25.300
Shou-chan...

00:21:30.050 --> 00:21:32.840
You planned that from the start...

00:21:32.840 --> 00:21:35.840
You have one coin left.

00:21:35.840 --> 00:21:37.400
And very little time.

00:21:38.860 --> 00:21:39.730
Here.

00:21:41.180 --> 00:21:41.860
What is it?

00:21:42.650 --> 00:21:44.610
A contract with the bookmaker.

00:21:45.850 --> 00:21:49.590
Are you really Morikawa?

00:21:51.030 --> 00:21:53.470
I'm finally me.

00:23:26.670 --> 00:23:28.770
Why not have fun?

00:23:27.890 --> 00:23:31.940
Wish. If I win, I want the puzzle pieces.

00:23:29.860 --> 00:23:31.530
The old you wouldn't have done this!

00:23:31.940 --> 00:23:33.450
It has nothing to do with you!

00:23:32.670 --> 00:23:33.990
I can't see the bottom of the darkness.

00:23:33.990 --> 00:23:37.000
You... You did that to Aya.

00:23:37.730 --> 00:23:41.020
Next time: Darkness / Fervent Desire and Loss.

00:23:37.930 --> 00:23:41.020
Darkness / Fervent Desire and Loss
